{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1770","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Koxia and Number Theory"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Joi has an array $$$a$$$ of $$$n$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"positive"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers. Koxia wants you to determine whether there exists a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"positive"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" integer $$$x \\gt 0$$$ such that $$$\\gcd(a_i+x,a_j+x)=1$$$ for all $$$1 \\leq i \\lt j \\leq n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Here $$$\\gcd(y, z)$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greatest_common_divisor"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"greatest common divisor (GCD)"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of integers $$$y$$$ and $$$z$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test consists of multiple test cases. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 100$$$) — the number of test cases. The description of test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\leq n \\leq 100$$$) — the size of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq a_i \\leq {10}^{18}$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$1000$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output \"YES\" (without quotes) if there exists a positive integer $$$x$$$ such that $$$\\gcd(a_i+x,a_j+x)=1$$$ for all $$$1 \\leq i \\lt j \\leq n$$$, and \"NO\" (without quotes) otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output the answer in any case (upper or lower). For example, the strings \"yEs\", \"yes\", \"Yes\", and \"YES\" will be recognized as positive responses."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n3\n5 7 10\n3\n3 3 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, we can set $$$x = 4$$$. This is valid because: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" When $$$i=1$$$ and $$$j=2$$$, $$$\\gcd(a_i+x,a_j+x)=\\gcd(5+4,7+4)=\\gcd(9,11)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" When $$$i=1$$$ and $$$j=3$$$, $$$\\gcd(a_i+x,a_j+x)=\\gcd(5+4,10+4)=\\gcd(9,14)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" When $$$i=2$$$ and $$$j=3$$$, $$$\\gcd(a_i+x,a_j+x)=\\gcd(7+4,10+4)=\\gcd(11,14)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, any choice of $$$x$$$ makes $$$\\gcd(a_1 + x, a_2 + x) = \\gcd(3+x,3+x)=3+x$$$. Therefore, no such $$$x$$$ exists."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1770C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1770/problem/C"}